1
00:00:01,510 --> 00:00:03,111
(Q1) SHIRLEY: Hello?&nbsp;

2
00:00:03,111 --> 00:00:09,042
TOM: Oh hello. I was hoping to speak to Jack Fitzgerald about renting a cottage.&nbsp;

3
00:00:09,042 --> 00:00:14,710
SHIRLEY: I'm his wife, Shirley, and we own the cottages together, so I'm sure I can help you.&nbsp;

4
00:00:14,710 --> 00:00:17,080
TOM: Great. My name's Tom.&nbsp;

5
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:22,659
Some friends of ours rented Granary Cottage from you last year, and they thought it was great.

6
00:00:22,659 --> 00:00:26,439
So my wife and I are hoping to come in May for a week.

7
00:00:26,439 --> 00:00:29,221
SHIRLEY: What date did you have in mind?&nbsp;

8
00:00:29,221 --> 00:00:51,698
[Q1答案句+ Q1干扰项] TOM: The week beginning the 14th, if possible.&nbsp;SHIRLEY: I'll just check ... I'm sorry, Tom, it's already booked that week.&nbsp; It's free the week beginning the 28th, though, for seven nights.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;In fact, that's the only time you could have it in May.

9
00:00:51,698 --> 00:00:54,896
We'd just need to change a couple of things.

10
00:00:54,896 --> 00:00:56,910
(Q2) How much would it cost?

11
00:00:56,910 --> 00:01:03,404
[Q2答案句] SHIRLEY: That's the beginning of high season, so it'd be ￡550 for the week.

12
00:01:03,404 --> 00:01:07,897
TOM: Ah. That's a bit more than we wanted to pay, I'm afraid.&nbsp;

13
00:01:07,897 --> 00:01:12,378
We've budgeted up to ￡500 for accommodation.

14
00:01:12,378 --> 00:01:20,265
(Q3) SHIRLEY: Well, we've just finished converting another building into a cottage, which we're calling Chervil Cottage.&nbsp;

15
00:01:20,265 --> 00:01:30,951
[Q3答案句] TOM: Sorry? What was that again?&nbsp;SHIRLEY: Chervil. C-H-E-R-V for Victor I-L.&nbsp;

16
00:01:30,951 --> 00:01:33,226
TOM: Oh, that's a herb, isn't it?

17
00:01:33,226 --> 00:01:36,865
SHIRLEY: That's right. It grows fairly wild around here.&nbsp;

18
00:01:36,865 --> 00:01:41,746
(Q4) You could have that for the week you want for ￡480.

19
00:01:41,746 --> 00:01:45,623
TOM: OK. So could you tell me something about it, please?&nbsp;

20
00:01:45,623 --> 00:01:50,410
[Q4答案句, was = originally] SHIRLEY: Of course. The building was built as a garage.&nbsp;

21
00:01:50,410 --> 00:01:53,386
It's a little smaller than Granary Cottage.

22
00:01:53,386 --> 00:01:55,807
(Q5) TOM: So that must sleep two people, as well?&nbsp;

23
00:01:55,807 --> 00:01:58,686
SHIRLEY: That's right. There's a double bedroom.&nbsp;

24
00:01:58,686 --> 00:02:07,245
[Q5答案句] TOM: Does it have a garden?SHIRLEY: Yes, you get to it from the living room through French doors, and we provide two deckchairs.&nbsp;

25
00:02:07,245 --> 00:02:13,777
(Q6) We hope to build a patio in the near future, but I wouldn't like to guarantee it'll be finished by May.

26
00:02:13,777 --> 00:02:14,844
TOM: OK.&nbsp;

27
00:02:14,844 --> 00:02:29,610
[Q6答案句] SHIRLEY: The front door opens onto the old farmyard, and parking isn't a problem – there's plenty of room at the front for that.&nbsp;

28
00:02:29,610 --> 00:02:33,160
(Q7) TOM: What about facilities in the cottage?

29
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:37,507
It has standard things like a cooker and fridge, I presume.

30
00:02:37,507 --> 00:02:44,445
SHIRLEY: In the kitchen area there's a fridge-freezer and we've just put in an electric cooker.

31
00:02:44,445 --> 00:02:46,554
Is there a washing machine?

32
00:02:46,554 --> 00:02:52,659
TOM: Yes. There's also a TV in the living room, which plays DVDs too.&nbsp;

33
00:02:52,659 --> 00:02:57,982
The bathroom is too small for a bath, so there's a shower instead.

34
00:02:57,982 --> 00:03:01,465
I think a lot of people prefer that nowadays, anyway.

35
00:03:01,465 --> 00:03:06,465
TOM: It's more environmentally friendly, isn't it?&nbsp; Unless you spend half the day in it!

36
00:03:06,465 --> 00:03:07,757
SHIRLEY: Exactly.&nbsp;

37
00:03:07,757 --> 00:03:12,499
[Q7定位词🟢] TOM: What about heating? It sometimes gets quite cool at that time of year.&nbsp;

38
00:03:12,499 --> 00:03:20,963
[Q7答案句] SHIRLEY: There's central heating, and if you want to light a fire, there's a stove.&nbsp; &nbsp;We can provide all the wood you need for it.

39
00:03:20,963 --> 00:03:28,116
[Q7干扰项] It smells so much nicer than coal, and it makes the room very cosy – we've got one in our own house.

40
00:03:28,116 --> 00:03:30,098
TOM: That sounds very pleasant.&nbsp;

41
00:03:30,098 --> 00:03:33,414
Perhaps we should come in the winter, to make the most of it!

42
00:03:33,414 --> 00:03:37,747
(Q8) SHIRLEY: Yes, we find we don't want to go out when we've got the fire burning.&nbsp;

43
00:03:37,747 --> 00:03:42,707
There are some attractive views from the cottage, which I haven't mentioned.

44
00:03:42,707 --> 00:03:50,191
[Q8答案句， oldest = old] There's a famous stone bridge – it's one of the oldest in the region, and you can see it from the living room.

45
00:03:50,191 --> 00:03:52,102
It isn't far away.

46
00:03:52,102 --> 00:03:59,938
(Q9) [Q9答案句] The bedroom window looks in the opposite direction, and has a lovely view of the hills and the monument at the top.

47
00:03:59,938 --> 00:04:02,773
(Q10) TOM: Well, that all sounds perfect.&nbsp;

48
00:04:02,773 --> 00:04:06,018
I'd like to book it, please. Would you want a deposit?

49
00:04:06,018 --> 00:04:15,177
SHIRLEY: Yes, we ask for thirty percent to secure your booking, so that'll be, um, ￡144.&nbsp;

50
00:04:15,177 --> 00:04:22,690
[Q10答案句] TOM: And when would you like the rest of the money?SHIRLEY: You're coming in May, so the last day of March, please.&nbsp;

51
00:04:22,690 --> 00:04:23,942
TOM: Fine.&nbsp;

52
00:04:23,942 --> 00:04:26,442
SHIRLEY: Excellent. Could I just take your details ...&nbsp;

